  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "China's construction cost economics (2-4× discount vs. Western) transfer to fusion capital accounts, applied broadly across CAS21-CAS26 not just buildings",
      "ITER-heritage Nb3Sn/NbTi LTS magnets at 6.15 T achieve commercial viability despite larger machine volume, offsetting higher per-kWe cost with lower $/kA-m conductor pricing",
      "CFETR Phase II DEMO-validation scenario (Pfus=1084 MW, Q=23.5 at R₀=6.6m, B₀=6.0T, Ip=11MA) is achievable in same hardware as Phase I via plasma current ramp-up",
      "sCO2 Brayton power conversion at 34.7% thermal efficiency is adopted for commercial PFPP, coupled via COOL (CO2-cooled LiPb) TBM lineage",
      "Four-method H&CD portfolio (ECRH+ICRH+LHCD+NBI) retains NBI for plasma rotation and direct ion heating — NBI removal drops Q by ~40% (2.0→1.2)",
      "TBM program (COOL/WCCB/EU) yields a viable commercial blanket achieving TBR>1.1 and self-sufficient tritium breeding at commercial NWL >1 MW/m²",
      "Quasi-steady-state long-pulse operation (>1000s, CF 75-90%) is achievable for commercial PFPP rather than inheriting CFETR's pulsed 30-50% duty cycle"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "REBCO HTS tape procurement bulk (5,000+ km for full-HTS architectures) — limited to CS sub-coils only, avoiding $0.75-1.6B full-HTS magnet system cost",
      "Novel/unqualified superconductor supply chain risk — Nb3Sn/NbTi are ITER-qualified with ASIPP domestic manufacturing (>70% of China's ITER packages)",
      "Tungsten material supply risk — China produces >80% of global tungsten, eliminating scarcity premium for first wall/divertor armor",
      "Western regulatory cost burden — Stewart & Shirvan 2.2× fission-style building cost factor may not apply in Chinese regulatory context",
      "High labor cost component of Western fusion construction — Chinese domestic labor rates and streamlined regulatory timelines cut infrastructure construction 2-4×"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Extrapolation premium across three additional development steps (BEST→CFEDR→PFPP) with commercial end-state unspecified, unlike private-sector concepts building toward defined products",
      "Concurrent four-method H&CD capital cost (50 MW: 15 ECRH + 10 ICRH + 10 LHCD + 12 NBI) substantially higher than single-technology approach, with LHCD potentially stranded at burning plasma temperatures",
      "Larger machine volume scaling for LTS route (R₀ = 6.6 m vs. ~1.85-3.6 m for compact HTS) drives ~5× magnet mass (~10,000 t) and vacuum vessel/structural steel scaling",
      "Helium refrigeration infrastructure at ITER scale (~40 kW at 4.5K, ~$1B) required for Nb3Sn operation — not needed for HTS-at-20K concepts",
      "TBM material qualification pipeline costs (RAFM steel, Li ceramics, SiCf/SiC, PbLi at nuclear-grade) — three competing concepts in parallel development until experimental down-selection"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Commercial PFPP design point (R, B, Q, Pfus, thermal efficiency, capital cost) entirely unspecified — all TEA outputs rest on ARIES-ACT1 and CFETR Phase I analogues rather than committed Chinese design",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Chinese construction cost discount magnitude for fusion is unproven — H1 hypothesis (2× discount halves LCOE) is untestable without Chinese cost benchmarks; regulatory cost framework opaque",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Blanket technology undecided among three competing TBM concepts (COOL/WCCB/EU) — blanket cost, TBR, coolant, and power cycle all unanchored until 2030s experimental results",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Capacity factor regime unknown — if PFPP inherits CFETR Phase I pulsed duty cycle (0.3-0.5), LCOE increases 1.5-3× vs. quasi-steady-state 75-90% assumption",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "CFETR Phase II readiness gaps: divertor heat load (Pdiv/R₀=32.4 MW/m) exceeds ITER guidelines, pellet injection fueling not implemented, RWM stabilization at βN=3.54 above no-wall limit unmodeled",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Commercial TBR >1.1 demonstration dependency on BEST TBM program (2030s) — failure cascades to self-sufficient tritium breeding and commercial viability; China lacks CANDU tritium access",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "LHCD applicability degraded in burning plasma — lower-hybrid accessibility is electron-temperature limited; NBI cannot be eliminated without ~40% Q penalty, constraining H&CD portfolio simplification",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Full-tungsten first wall + divertor integration at Q~5 D-T burning plasma is unprecedented — ELM mitigation and W impurity control in high-alpha-heating regime not demonstrated",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "YBCO CS sub-coil performance at 18.8T peak field under cyclic thermal/mechanical loads and D-T neutron flux (~0.04 dpa lifetime) not validated at BEST scale",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Gross-to-net electric ratio degradation at smaller plant sizes (17% at 100 MWe vs. 42% at 1.2 GWe) makes first-of-kind PFPP at 500 MWe sensitive to recirculating power assumptions from four-method H&CD",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium permeation through CO2-facing heat exchangers in COOL/sCO2 coupling requires unvalidated permeation barriers; sCO2 as oxidizing medium differs from inert He coolant strategy",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "description": "SiCf/SiC composite manufacturing scalability (TRL 3-4 globally) for COOL TBM flow channel inserts unproven at commercial scale",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ]
  },
